## Reproduced defect (unreleased PR #2)

Tested **20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b**, package 2026.10.18, Node 24.19.0, pinned @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.18. This concerns the implementation in [PR #2](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/2), not the scaffold currently on main.

A typed model failure in an already-created child is converted into a parent tool refusal. The parent can then finish successfully, but the persisted call graph contains an unfinished child. Replay rejects that successfully completed run, and resume returns the root answer without repairing or retrying the child.

## Source goal

The [canonical epic](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b/.agents/pm/epics/pm-rlm-a1ih.toon) requires durable budgets, crash resume and replay. The [README](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b/README.md) promises replay of the recorded actions with a byte-identical answer and recoverable tool refusals.

## Sanitized reproduction

Use a temporary SDK tracker and deterministic model only; no provider, network inference, credentials or existing tracker data are needed. At the tested checkout, save this as a temporary test at the repository root and execute `node --test review-repro.test.ts` (remove it before repository-wide lint):

```ts
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { test } from 'node:test';
import { tracker, ScriptedModel } from './test/helpers.ts';
import { runRlm, replayRlm, resumeRlm, treeRlm } from './src/engine.ts';
import { RlmError } from './src/errors.ts';
import { PROTOCOL } from './src/protocol.ts';

test('failed child leaves a successful run unreplayable', async t => {
  const { workspace } = await tracker(t);
  const model = new ScriptedModel(request => {
    const input = JSON.parse(request.prompt.slice(PROTOCOL.length + 1));
    if (input.depth === 1) throw new RlmError('model', 'Transient offline model');
    return JSON.stringify(input.transcript.length
      ? { action: 'finish', answer: 'recovered' }
      : { action: 'spawn', subgoal: 'child',
          slice: { fragments: [], estimated_tokens: 2 } });
  });
  const result = await runRlm('root', { workspace, model });
  assert.equal(result.answer, 'recovered');
  await assert.rejects(replayRlm(workspace, result.run), {
    code: 'replay', message: 'Recorded call graph has unreachable calls'
  });
  assert.equal((await resumeRlm(workspace, result.run, model)).answer, 'recovered');
  const tree = await treeRlm(workspace, result.run);
  assert.deepEqual(tree.calls.map(call => call.status), ['closed', 'in_progress']);
});
```

Observed: the regression test passes, proving the undesirable behavior. The successful run reports 2 calls; the root is closed and the child remains in progress even after resume. The same observation was repeated with telemetry disabled and isolated HOME.

## Cause and impact

- [spawn](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b/src/engine.ts#L73-L81) persists the child before executing it
- [execute's catch](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b/src/engine.ts#L121-L126) catches any nested RlmError and stores only `{refused: code}`
- Replay skips refused steps, then rejects the unvisited child; resume sees the completed root and returns without resuming that child

A transient endpoint error during recursion therefore breaks replay/recovery guarantees even when the top-level command reports success. This is distinct from the existing oversized-read/context-limit review: an empty child slice and ordinary typed transport failure suffice.

## Expected behavior / regression criteria

Define a durable outcome for materialized children when their spawn fails. Either propagate an interrupted child as a resumable run failure, or record a terminal failed child and replay that refusal consistently. A root reported as successful must remain replayable, and resume must not report recovery while silently leaving an orphaned in-progress child. Add coverage for child transport failure and context refusal after child creation, preserving reservation accounting and existing SIGKILL/digest-reuse behavior.

## Scope and deduplication

Reviewed all-status issues/PRs (#1–3), PR #2's 10 existing inline comments/review, and the eight canonical tracker records at this commit. No matching failed-child/replay record was present. This is a deterministic local reproduction; no live-provider quality, Bun acceptance, release readiness or deployed behavior is claimed.


