### GitHub comments (2)

> **@unbraind** (2026-10-19T05:20:07Z)
>
> Additional terminal-child evidence on PR #2, exact head `7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba`: a transient SDK read failure during child completion can now be swallowed as a tool refusal, allowing a successful root to leave its completed child `in_progress`.
> 
> The canonical [ledger feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/.agents/pm/features/pm-rlm-6a8t.toon) requires Task evidence and a matching call graph. The PR explicitly promises evidence, closure and claim release for every child in a successfully returned run. The original transport-failure path reported in this issue is repaired; this is a new completion-read regression against the same terminal-child invariant, distinct from the repaired history-read and comment-write cases. Explicit resume does repair this new case, so the older non-recoverability claim does not apply.
> 
> Cause:
> - The newly added `sdkRead` around [materialize's complete-list read](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/src/ledger.ts#L105-L121) converts an unexpected SDK error into `RlmError('incomplete')`
> - A child finish is already checkpointed when `complete()` invokes that read. [spawn](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/src/engine.ts#L91-L100) sees `call.result` and rethrows without repairing evidence
> - The parent's [generic typed-error catch](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/src/engine.ts#L148-L164) records `{refused:'incomplete'}` and continues. Terminal reconciliation runs [before root execution only](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/src/engine.ts#L169-L181)
> 
> Reproduction: a real SDK-created synthetic tracker and scripted parent/child model. Once the child's finish response is produced, a one-shot wrapper around `PmClient.prototype.listAllComplete` creates a directory named `tasks/review-unreadable.toon`, calls the original SDK method, and removes the directory in `finally`. Thus the SDK itself produces a real filesystem-read error; the wrapper supplies neither a fabricated SDK result nor a fabricated exception. All other SDK operations remain real.
> 
> Actual on this head: `runRlm` returns `answer:'root success', calls:2`. Root item is closed; child has durable `result:'child success'` but remains `in_progress`. Parent's spawn observation is `{refused:'incomplete'}`. Replay already returns the recorded root answer despite the open SDK child. Calling resume explicitly repairs and closes the child without a second child inference. The observed defect is incomplete terminal evidence/closure at successful return, not an unreplayable or permanently stranded run.
> 
> Control: the identical fault on prior head `cdac605b19b95ac02caed2d96c83f1e9c080f2e6` aborts the root with no root result or parent observation. Resume then repairs the child and finishes with one total child inference. This demonstrates a regression in the new typed-read classification rather than a failure of the test fixture.
> 
> Expected/regression criteria: completion-reconciliation failures must not be converted into a successful tool refusal while evidence remains unfinished. Either abort and preserve the unfinished parent observation until resume repairs it, or reconcile every terminal child before returning success. Cover transient errors at both reads in completion, then verify actual SDK Task closure/evidence/claim release, replay, and no repeat inference after recovery. Keep malformed source history as a recoverable read refusal and preserve the separate fatal evidence-write regression.
> 
> Validation limits: fresh typecheck and all 113 unit tests pass; 46 non-install behavioral revert proofs pass. The two packed-install proofs were intentionally not rerun because they install dependencies. Isolated copied source was verified against immutable Git blob identities. No provider calls, credentials, dependency changes, original-checkout modifications, or live integrations were used. The reproduction uses deterministic timing instrumentation at the SDK boundary, not a claim that this transient filesystem condition happened in production.
> 

> **@unbraind** (2026-10-19T07:02:00Z)
>
> Post-merge verification: the completion-read case in [the preceding report](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/issues/4#issuecomment-6260265599) still reproduces on exact main/PR #2 merge commit `90b99a0952f175d4732a133def5d83935db0bbfb`, after this issue was closed.
> 
> I reran the unchanged real-SDK filesystem-fault reproduction on a separately materialized copy verified against all 104 tracked Git blobs. It returns `answer:'root success', calls:2`; the root is closed, but the child has `result:'child success'` and remains `in_progress`. The parent records `{refused:'incomplete'}`. Replay returns the answer; explicit resume closes the child with one total child inference.
> 
> The relevant path is unchanged: [completion reads](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90b99a0952f175d4732a133def5d83935db0bbfb/src/ledger.ts#L105-L130) can become typed refusals through [the parent catch](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90b99a0952f175d4732a133def5d83935db0bbfb/src/engine.ts#L149-L165), while [terminal reconciliation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90b99a0952f175d4732a133def5d83935db0bbfb/src/engine.ts#L170-L182) occurs only before execution. This remains the previously reported incomplete terminal-evidence/closure case, not a claim that replay or explicit recovery is broken.
> 
> Please retain this residual case as open work: either propagate completion failure until resume repairs it, or reconcile terminal children before returning success, with coverage for both completion reads. No provider calls, dependency changes or production data were used.
